=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
# firewall screen-lockout-at-start -----------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Mock: The Firewall screen. web-01.example.net runs Debian 13.$
# sshd on 2230, ufw stopped with ENABLED=yes, its saved rules$
# allowing 443 alone: the next boot refuses SSH. hardn refuses$
# to plan over the disagreement.$
$
# UFW Firewall Configuration ###################################$
$
  [ ] Firewall             Not Configured enabled, not running$
$
# ufw ----------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [+] Installed            Yes$
  [ ] Status               Inactive$
   -  Incoming policy      Deny$
  [+] At boot              Yes$
$
# SSH ----------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [ ] [::]:2230            Refused at start$
  [ ] 0.0.0.0:2230         Refused at start$
$
# Rules --------------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  443/tcp              Allow Saved$
   -  443/tcp (v6)         Allow Saved$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Enable firewall      Let SSH through, then start ufw$
   2) Application Profiles Add, remove, apply$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter selection [0-2 or q]:$
$
$

